Downloaded from: https://https.git.savannah.gnu.org/git/bash.git
Listed at: https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/bug-bash/2026-10/msg00015.html
Upstream commit: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/bash.git/commit/?id=2f7eb80c770c13adaabca4d6bf4ba5c01a01244d

Follow-up correction for upstream GNU Bash patch bash53-019.

Patch bash53-019 changed legal_variable_starter() and legal_variable_char()
to use the sh_syntaxtab character table. parameter_brace_expand() passed a
plain char to legal_variable_starter(), allowing a high-bit input byte to
become a negative table index on systems with signed char.

Backport the subst.c correction from the upstream 2026-08-17 commit:
convert that input byte to unsigned char before checking the variable name.

Original upstream patch: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/bash/bash-5.3-patches/bash53-019
Original report: https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/bug-bash/2026-08/msg00025.html

The 019a filename applies this backport immediately after bash53-019.patch.
The GNU patch level remains 20.

diff --git subst.c subst.c
index f54459a..f22a553 100644
--- subst.c
+++ subst.c
@@ -10121,7 +10121,7 @@ parameter_brace_expand (char *string, size_t *indexp, int quoted, int pflags, in
   sindex = *indexp;
   t_index = ++sindex;
   /* ${#var} doesn't have any of the other parameter expansions on it. */
-  if (string[t_index] == '#' && legal_variable_starter (string[t_index+1]))		/* {{ */
+  if (string[t_index] == '#' && legal_variable_starter ((unsigned char)string[t_index+1]))		/* {{ */
     name = string_extract (string, &t_index, "}", SX_VARNAME);
   else
 #if defined (CASEMOD_EXPANSIONS)
